        "hash": "62e41a2e42b538bbb08f49ac020ab3edf2052d67",
        "subject": "fix(portal): a refused payment proof says why; the payer number is never cut",
        "body": "fix(portal): a refused payment proof says why; the payer number is never cut\n\nA file identical to an approved proof was refused (409 proof_duplicate) and every 409 read as 'somebody else changed\nthis'. Each proof refusal now has its own words (duplicate, already waiting, request reused, decided, revised); only a\nproof that really changed reads as a change. One save sends one request, even with Enter pressed twice.\n\nThe payer field drops separators and an explicit +222/00222 before eight digits; nothing is truncated, a wrong length\ngets the form's own message (no browser pattern tooltip). An eight-digit number beginning with 222 is kept.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
        "author": {
          "name": "CLAUDE",
          "email": "abdelkerim.mahfoudh@gmail.com",
          "time": 1794526468000
        },
